# privateConfig — do not edit on program changes

**Rule Rev.1** — 2026-09-13 (DialKey)

When changing DialKey **program** code, spec, or shared docs, **do not edit
privateConfig** or other personal runtime config. Measure in an isolated
folder (`_measure/`, `dist/`), not the user's running install.

## Do not touch

- Any path or folder named **`privateConfig`**
- Other `.cursor/rules/private_*` (gitignored), except **`private_spec.md`**
  when the user asked or when moving author-only notes out of `docs/spec.md`
- Personal slot books (`slots.json`, `slots.*.json` except `slots.example.json`)
- A live install's `settings/` (for example `Now on running\...\settings\`)

## Do edit

- `config/settings.json`, `config/slots.example.json`, `lang/*.toml`
- Public spec / docs site / `.cursor/rules/` that are **not** `private_*`
- `.cursor/rules/private_spec.md` only for author-only notes (never commit)

Personal JSON is the user's machine, not the product. Never commit it.
